Mortar (TrimUI Brick) changes to digdat0/ACGC-Switch-Port, all behind
TARGET_MORTAR (pkgs/acgc/CMakeLists.txt defines it with TARGET_ANDROID):

- libultra.h: glibc declares bcmp/bcopy/bzero (mortar_decls.h includes them).
- pc_main.c: load GLES through SDL_GL_GetProcAddress (compat/glad/gl.h).
- pc_gx_tev.c + default.frag: specialized fragment shaders get the TEV
  stages as straight-line GLSL generated from the key (acTev) and sample
  textures straight from the varyings. The PowerVR compiler neither unrolls
  the stage loop nor folds the helper switches (and fails on them inlined at
  literal indices), so every pixel ran the whole TEV interpreter: the title
  screen took ~55 ms of GPU per frame at 640x480, now ~5 ms at 1024x768.
  Plus the Switch build's program binary cache (~70 s of shader compiles at
  every start without it).
- pc_gx.c: the Switch build's vertex ring (one 8 MiB buffer, base-vertex
  draws), persistently mapped with EXT_buffer_storage: glBufferData per
  draw made the PowerVR driver allocate and map device memory each time.
- pc_gx_texture.c: the Switch build's compact texture formats and mip
  chains (decoded on the main thread; no decode thread).
- pc_keybindings.c, pc_pad.c, pc_pause_menu.c: Brick buttons by label; the
  D-pad drives the main stick, L2 + D-pad is the GameCube D-pad, L2 + the
  face buttons the C-stick (documented in keybindings.ini).
- neosthread.c: no [NEOS_OUT] audio diagnostic every second.
- pc_vi.c: ACGC_FPS=1 logs the frame rate.

